{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1458674-1001-wraith-npcs-character-concepts","id":1458674,"title":"1001 Wraith NPCs & character concepts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-04T07:34:42-07:00","id":1458674,"title":"1001 Wraith NPCs & character concepts","content":"<span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A topic to share characters that could be useful or inspiration for our Wraith chronicles. Every level of detail is welcome. I'll start with this major NPC I wrote this week for an upcoming WtO game:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>1. </b></span></span></span><b>Thomas B\u00f6rner, Emerald Anacreon</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A political mastermind who governs from his church Haunt beyond the northern frontier of the Leipzig Necropolis. For about two centuries now Thomas is the ranking Emerald official here, making him one of Leipzig's longest serving Anacreons. And although power still firmly rests with the Grim Legion, he's undoubtedly the most respected local Hierarch as well. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thomas lived during the first half of the 17th century in what was then the village of Mockau, having since become part of the city. The son of a miller, he followed in his father's footsteps and married a beautiful girl. Unfortunately Thomas came of age during the Thirty Years' War. Although feeling little appetite for leaving his young wife and daughter, the local pastor made a convincing argument. Telling the young man it was his duty to God to protect Lutheranism against the Catholic hordes. In taking up arms for his faith he and his family would earn divine protection.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In his years away from home, fighting under Swedish command, Thomas did feel protected. Never suffering any serious injuries, while he saw countless others perish. When finally being able to return to Mockau he was horrified to learn the pastor's promise had in fact not held up. During Thomas' absence the bubonic plague had ravaged the village. His parents, his wife, his child, they were all gone. Ditched in a mass grave only a few weeks before his return. Thomas felt betrayed by God and the pastor that spoke for Him. The furious soldier went to the church looking to mete out his revenge on the clergyman. Only to discover he had long since been buried as well. Thomas instead screamed at the heavens, cursing God as a storm was brewing. Only moments later the raging blasphemer was struck down by a bolt of lightning.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Enfant had a Reaper from the Legion of Fate waiting for him. Once the situation was explained, Thomas vehemently refused to be inducted into that particular Legion. Insisting that his death was purely accidental, completely rejecting a higher power like fate or God. After arriving in Stygia, the Emerald Legion took possession of him instead. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A couple of decades later he returned to Leipzig's Shadowlands as a Legionnaire. Part of a Stygian force that was to establish a Necropolis there. Sadly Thomas was unable to find any trace of his family. Which only made him fight that much harder, knowing who to blame. Years of religious strife had left the area a hive of heresy that was to be eradicated. The Legionnaire took particular pleasure in tracking down his former pastor, sending him to the forges. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">As the Necropolis grew, Thomas was dismayed to see the local Hierarchy's stance on Heretics softening over time. Multiple Circles of them were left in peace as long they didn't draw too much attention to themselves. This served as the impetus for the ambitious Lemure's long rise through the ranks. Hoping to one day find himself in a position where he could dictate a zero-tolerance policy toward heresy.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thomas finally achieved the rank of Anacreon in the wake of the Battle of Nations, after his predecessor lost the last of his Fetters. Unfortunately the astounding number of casualties also confirmed the Grim Anacreon as absolute ruler of the Necropolis. The influence any other Legion would have would be negligible at best. Except if one of those other Anacreons were to be a particularly shrewd politician. Exactly what Thomas has developed into over the last couple of centuries. Becoming especially effective in the post-war period. As the Fifth Great Maelstrom left the Leipzig Grim Legion with a far younger and less experienced leader. With all his schemes starting to pay off, it looks like Anacreon B\u00f6rner might finally get his way.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Image:</b> A well-built figure wearing a wide-brimmed hat and 1630s soldier garb. As to command further respect from the ubiquitous Grim Legion, he always has a sword of Stygian steel buckled to his side. As well as wearing a skeleton mask similar in style to the helmets worn by the Grim military. Under the mask is the face of a man in his early twenties, sporting a moustache and short beard. Thomas' most fetching feature are his compassionate hazel eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You hate God, in your opinion it's just another guise of Oblivion. He's the entity that's taken everything from you, who you fear and hate. However centuries of politicking have taught not to reveal your true feelings about anything. Everyone should instead have the impression that you're on their side. Which means you rarely give a straight answer to any question. Your soft spot for women and children is the only aspect of your true motives you've been unable to hide entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Fanatic<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Mediator<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina (Enduring) 4<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 3, Manipulation (Persuasive) 5, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 3, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 2, Athletics 1, Brawl 2, Empathy 2, Expression 2, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 3, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Etiquette 2, Firearms 3, Leadership 3, Melee 2, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Bureaucracy 3, Enigmas 1, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Politics (Hierarchy) 4<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 4, Artifact 3, Contacts 3, Eidolon 3, Haunt 4, Notoriety 3, Status 5<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Argos 1, Fatalism 4, Outrage 3<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Be in control of own fate (Fear) 3, Protect women and children (Love) 1, Stamp out heresy (Hate) 4<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Stephanus Church of Mockau 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 12-17-2021, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T20:46:30-07:00","id":1466599,"title":"","content":"Good description. I just subscribed to this post, because I am planning to include at least one Wraith Character in my Mage Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T04:03:19-08:00","id":1470700,"title":"","content":"<b>2. F. W. Murnau, the filmmaker's phantom:</b><br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/malkafian/art/F-W-Murnau-the-filmmaker-s-phantom-880618987\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/malkafian...ntom-880618987</a><br /> <br /> (more of a crossover character)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T02:21:00-08:00","id":1474113,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>3. Antoon Duval, Hunter of T<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">he Hun</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The leader of Les Patriotes, a Renegade group that hunts the former battlefields in the West of Flanders for the ghosts of enemy combatants. Now since the onset of the Second World War he's looking to drive off German forces in the Skinlands as well. Antoon sees his great-granddaughterAnna as a means to that end.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Back when the rural Flemish village of Beselare was still the Marquisate Beselare, the Duvals were one of its most prominent families. Second only to the marquises themselves, who for generations they served as bailiffs. A glory period that ended with the French Revolution, half a century before Antoon was born. Stories the boy was raised on, teaching him to be proud of his family and how important they'd been to their village. Lessons which led to his decision to study medicine. Becoming a country doctor was not the most prestigious vocation a young man of his intellect could achieve. However he knew it was a role he'd be respected for in his local community like few other men were.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Never straying far from home, Antoon's life would be far from adventurous. Filled with happiness though. He married, had many children, then came grandchildren. Only in those final years did things turn sour. Antoon lost his wife, also the physical ability to keep practicing medicine. And then the Great War erupted. Beselare lay right between Ypres and the advancing German army. The entire village was forcibly evacuated. Antoon didn't want to go, but was too feeble to resist. As a living man he'd never see his home again. Less than two weeks later he'd been buried in Northern France. A rural gravesite that would be lost during the course of the war.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">After Antoon's death the Enfant was swiftly Reaped and put in chains. Spending the next couple of years as a Thrall of the Douai Necropolis. When the Night of the Short Chains occurred he was able to use the chaos to escape. Antoon braved the Great Maelstrom, gradually making his way home. In the Skinlands his village was no more. The Beselare he remembered was by then a ghost like Antoon himself. Sheltering in these Rel<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">ic buildings were both familiar faces, many former patients, as well as foreign soldiers. It was Antoon who was instrumental in rallying Beselare's wraith in defense of their home against the Maelstrom and the many Spectres. When those threats had subsided he turned on the German Restless in their midst. Souls he'd previously fought alongside with were sold off for weaponry. That had always been Antoon's plan.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">A couple of decades later Beselare is Renegade fortress existing in an uneasy peace with the nearby Necropoli of Ypres, Kortrijk and Roeselare. It's an open secret that several local Anacreons support Les Patriotes. Primarily cause these Renegades' depredations are seen as a check on the Grim Legion's power. </span>But also because German and Austro-Hungarian wraiths are simply detested by much of the native Restless Dead. Besides Hierarchs, Antoon has good relations with the Masquers Guild as well, to which he owes his hunting pack of barghests. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Image:</b> Nothing like the decrepit old man he died as. His Corpus is that of a man in his prime, be it a white-bearded one. Appears well-dressed in turn of the century black suit and tie. When out hunting he brandishes a soulsteel hunting knife in his right hand. While in the left Antoon holds the leash to four vicious barghests. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You're an old fashioned gentleman. Charismatic, yet obviously ruthless. With but few exceptions you consider all Belgians to be decent people. Germans and their ilk are all awful, with no exceptions. Hunting down their souls and condemning them to the forges is a pleasure. While for the dead of Beselare you'll fight till Oblivion takes you.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Activist<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Leader<br /> <b>Physical:</b>Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social:</b>Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Mental:</b>Perception 3, Intelligence 4, Wits 4<br /> <b>Talents:</b>Alertness 1, Brawl 2, Empathy 1,Expression 1, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 3, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b>Crafts 1, Etiquette 3, Firearms 2, Leadership 3,Melee 2, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 2, Bureaucracy 1, Medicine 3, Occult , Politics 1, Science 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b>Allies 5, Artifact 2, Contacts 4, Eidolon 2, Haunt 4, Memoriam 2, Notoriety 3, Status 5<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Argos 1, Lifeweb 2, Moliate 2<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Destroy the invaders (Anger) 4, Support descendants (Pride) 3<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Physical Remains 3, Wife's Wedding Ring 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Pathos:</b> 7<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 8<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 7</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 02-08-2022, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T11:30:05-08:00","id":1474813,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>4. Jan van Speyk, the Sea Beggars' last hope</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">A Renegade captain sailing the Shadowland reflection of the English Channel. Continuously on the lookout for relic ships to salvage, as to counteract the swift decline of the Sea Beggars. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally an orphan from Amsterdam who during the early 19<sup>th</sup> century worked himself up in the Royal Netherlands Navy. Jan served in the Dutch East Indies from 1823 to 1825. Successfully attacking Bangka and Java, which earned him the nickname &quot;Terror of the Bandits&quot;. During the Belgian Revolution, lieutenant commander van Speyk was given command of a gunboat deployed on the Scheldt river. In the winter of 1831, a gale had his crew lose control of the vessel. They drifted off toward Antwerp where the boat was besieged by a mob of Belgians. Rather than surrendering Jan instead threw his cigar into a barrel of gunpowder. In the resultant explosion all but 3 of his 30 subordinates perished, as well as a number of Belgian rebels.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">In the Skinlands the Dutch hailed van Speyk as a naval hero. His physical remains, sans head, were recovered to be buried with honors in Amsterdam. Jan's Underworld reception was far less welcoming. His former crew felt betrayed by their commanding officer's actions, these wraiths wanted revenge. The Grim Legion was happy to oblige, putting van Speyk on trial for murder. Condemned to be soulforged into an ashtray, if not for the intervention by the Sea Beggars. These were seafaring Renegades who regularly raided Necropoli along the coast and major rivers of the Low Countries. Dutch nationalists who wished to add this fallen hero to their ranks. Besides freeing the convict they also made off with the relic of his gunboat.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Over the next century or so van Speyk took great pleasure in ransacking the Necropoli of the upstart Belgians. Until the Sea Beggars started rapidly declining in the wake of the Second World War. With all the relic battleships they'd recovered the Stygian navy had grown vastly more potent, overpowering the Renegades' fleet at every turn. With van Speyk being one of the senior Sea Beggars remaining in the Shadowlands, he feels obligated to improve their lot. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Image:</b> An average looking man of about 30. Jan's eyes are pale blue, his hair and sideburns are brown. Jan's clad in a dark blue naval uniform, to our modern eyes Napoleonic era in style.A Stygian steel saber hangs from his belt. Between the fingers of his right hand the wraith's always holding a smoking cigar. This is not a relic, but a permanent touch of Oblivion on van Speyk's Corpus.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints: </b>Prone to give grand speeches, preaching about country and faith. Within you're still marked by your humble beginnings though. Eager to prove yourself in the eyes of God and wraith. Never showing guilt about the things you've done, it all serves a greater, yet unknown, purpose. Perhaps Transcendence will be your final reward?<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Competitor<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Fanatic<br /> <b>Physical: </b>Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social: </b>Charisma 4, Manipulation 4, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Mental: </b>Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents: </b>Alertness 2, Athletics 2, Brawl 1,Expression 1, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Boating 4, Crafts (Tailoring) 2, Etiquette 2, Firearms 3, Leadership 3,Meditation 1, Melee 3, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Enigmas 1,Medicine 1, Politics 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b>Allies 4, Artifact 3, Contacts 3, Eidolon 2, Memoriam 5, Notoriety 3, Relic 5, Status 5<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Argos 5, Fatalism 2<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Prove to be a worthy commander (Pride) 5, Have head reunited with other remains (Faith) 1<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Gunboat's Mast 4, Skull 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Pathos:</b> 9</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 8</span><br /> <b>Shadow:</b> The Martyr<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Thorns:</b> Death's Sigil, Infamy, Shadow Call<br /> <b>Shadow Passions:</b> Dive into a Nihil (Self-Hatred) 3, Kill Belgians (Hate) 2, Sink ships (Greed) 2</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 03-02-2022, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T10:06:53-08:00","id":1475540,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>5. Marie Masereel, the waifish Reaper</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A Skeletal socialite who has her Haunt in the Blankenberge Necropolis. She supports her lavish afterlifestyle by freelance Reaping throughout much of Flanders' Shadowlands.<br /> The girl grew up among the moneyed elite in late 19<sup>th</sup> century Antwerp. Tragically she contracted tuberculosis during her teens. Though for years treatment kept the disease under control, she was unable to lead a normal life. Her formative years were spent in isolation from the world she yearned to join. Most of the time Marie's only companionship was her governess, also serving as a nurse. Much of her final years were spent away from home, at the family residence on the Belgian coast in Blankenberge, taking in the fresh air. It was during such a stay that consumption finally claimed her.<br /> As a wraith Marie originally kept her distance from the Hierarchy. Until after the Great War broke out, when she volunteered for active duty in the Skeletal Legion. Fighting alongside her baby brother, who in his middle age had succumbed to the Spanish Flu. Marie eventually climbed to the rank of Centurion, her brother unfortunately fell to Oblivion. She hopes to one day redeem his soul. Part of her wider objective to reclaim the life she never had, in the Underworld. Hence why she left active military service to pursue a career in Reaping. Providing her with the contacts and funds to gather Masereel souls, creating a close-knit family from those few loved ones that became wraiths as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A face which is the romantic ideal of consumption; pale with rosy cheeks. Marie's pallor forming a perfect contrast to her dark hair, slightly damp with sweat. This wraith generally appears in the white nightgown she died in. The only real color her Corpus shows are the spatters of coughed up blood on her chest. This is only her day-to-day attire though. Marie owns a wide selection of lavish gowns, souls expertly Moliated by Masquer craftswraiths. She slides one of these over her Corpus whenever attending a ball or other social function. She's generally not shy about her profession, only rarely leaving her Haunt without carrying Reaper's Chains and having a barghest at her side.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints: </b>Old fashioned or what some might describe as an entitled brat. You believe in class. That there's an order to both the Skinlands and the Underworld, which puts people or wraiths like you at the top. Illness kept you from enjoying your god-given privileges, you're determined to seize them in death.<br /> You'll at first approach them as an angel, yet you feel no pity towards Thralls. You love your family, you respect Hierarchs, anyone else is fair game.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Traditionalist<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Rogue<br /> <b>Physical: </b>Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social: </b>Charisma 2, Manipulation 4, Appearance 4<br /> <b>Mental: </b>Perception 3, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents: </b>Alertness 2, Brawl 1, Empathy 1, Expression 1, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills: </b>Etiquette 3, Leadership 3, Meditation 1, Melee 2, Performance (Piano) 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 2, Bureaucracy 1, Enigmas 1, Investigation 1, Politics 1, Science 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds: </b>Allies 4, Artifact 3, Contacts 5, Eidolon 4, Haunt 3, Notoriety 2, Relic 4, Status 2<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Argos 2, Keening 2, Moliate 1, Outrage 3<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Recapture the life she missed out on (Bitterness) 4, Protect souls of kin (Love) 4<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Blankenberge Residence 4, Family Tomb 3, Porcelain Doll 1<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Pathos:</b> 5<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 5</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 02-27-2022, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T16:49:26-07:00","id":1480221,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>6. Ivo, the Outsider</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sometimes a lonely child is comforted by what they'd used to describe as a goblin. However kids these days generally believe it's an alien entering their bedroom at night. Ivo's no extraterrestrial though and he certainly doesn't come in peace.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">During the 1930s he was born in Berlin to the newlywed Stoltzes. Because of complications during the pregnancy Ivo was to remain their only child. Unfortunately Frieda Stoltz's difficult labor had also affected her boy's health. In the enfant's first months he developed hydrocephalus; fluid build-up within his brain. After a year of treatment the baby's condition was finally under control. But his enlarged skull would forever mark Ivo as being different, a dangerous thing in Nazi Germany. His father was a party member himself, though fought for his son to be treated right. Putting everything on the line when against the state's wishes he insisted Ivo get a normal education, not be shipped off to some institution. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Although Ivo was of normal intelligence, he had an awful time at school. Ostracized by students and teachers both, who saw him as subhuman. The loneliness this caused took a terrible toll on the boy. Yet far worse was still to come during the war.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">One morning while Ivo was walking to school his home was hit by an air raid. With no family left who'd defend him, the boy's fate now rested in the Nazi regime's hands. As part of the T4 Program the authorities sent him to the D\u00f6sen Sanatorium in Leipzig. Their disabled children's wing had only one real objective; murder. Some young patients were outright killed, many were experimented on, all were withheld proper care. Not receiving enough food Ivo slowly starved to death. After which as a final indignity the attending doctor removed his head to be preserved in a jar of formaldehyde.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ivo's head was first brought to the medical university in Berlin. Where it would remain until taken by looters when the Third Reich fell. Since that time the jar has moved from one private collection to another. Closely followed by a Spectral Ivo who does not take kindly to his physical remains being treated as a curio piece. The offending collectors tend to befall terrible accidents and children go missing.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Image:</b> A sickly child of about eight years in age. His emaciated Corpus is naked except for a pair of stained briefs. Decades of Spectrehood have further warped the size of Ivo's cranium, the shaved scalp has multiple tears revealing the bone underneath. His sockets lack eyes, within instead burns the black fire of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints: </b>For a Spectre you're unusually preoccupied by the Skinlands. Wraiths have little to fear, it's living children who're your focus. Approaching them as a friendly visitor from another world. They're of course unaware that you aren't describing an alien planet, but the Underworld. You gradually attempt to win their confidence, culminating in you luring them away for what you consider to be the ultimate bonding experience: Trapping them in a remote place to starve as you did.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Deviant<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Caregiver<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 1, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 4, Manipulation 4, Appearance 1<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 1, Athletics 1, Awareness 1, Brawl 1, Empathy 2, Expression 1, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Crafts 1, Etiquette 1, Larceny 1, Leadership 1, Meditation 1, Stealth 3<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Enigmas 2<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Memoriam 2, Shadowlands 3</span></span><br /> <b>Dark </b><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Arcanoi:</b> Corruption 2, Maleficence 4, Shroud Rending 3, Tempestos 1<br /> <b>Shadecraft:</b> Ectoplasmic Tentacles<br /> <b>Dark Passions:</b> Trap and starve children (Loneliness) 5, Punish those who disrespect his remains (Hate) 3<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> D\u00f6sen Sanatorium Building 2, Preserved Head 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Pathos:</b> 3<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 8<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 9<br /> <b>Merits/Flaws:</b> Endless Hunger, Penetrating Glare</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 05-26-2022, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T10:30:50-07:00","id":1484881,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>7. Hubert the hue</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A Restless resident of the NextWorld offices in Berlin. When not on missions he can usually be found there watching television. Unless of course he's out slumming the city's pigment hotspots.<br /> Hubert Wagner originally hails from a rural village south of Leipzig, Germany. An economically desolate area during the 1990s, his parents were rarely employed. Hence why the boy grew up relatively poor. Getting into mischief with his friends was one of the few divergences he could afford. The back of the old cemetery became a favored hangout spot to those kids. Right next to an old Napoleonic war memorial is where Hubert smoked his first cigarette, drank his first can of beer, felt up his first girl,... By their mid-teens these youngsters had graduated to weed, occasionally experimenting with something stronger. So it was that at one time a friend of Hubert's returned from Berlin with a baggie of pigment. Soon enough each teen there snorted a line, right off their favorite war monument.<br /> If one just wanted a relaxing high, they couldn't have picked a worse spot to try black heroin. The village's wraithly society centered around that very same graveyard. As the drug started kicking in, a couple of dozen strange figures came into view. Staring right at them, trying to gain Pathos from the hot-blooded teens, as these wraiths had done hundreds of times before. Panic broke out, all the drug-addled Quick fled the scene. Except Hubert, like always wanting to be the toughest of the bunch. Not truly believing what he was seeing, the young man was able to get a grip on his terror. Demonstrating his cockiness by striking up a conversation with the prettiest face among the dour crowd. She was a maiden wearing clothing centuries out of date. Eager to tell her tale of woe to someone who could help.<br /> By the time the pigment wore off Hubert had accepted what he'd experienced; a real ghost girl was in need of his assistance. Kornelia had never gotten a proper burial. Her murderers had hidden away her body, trapping her soul on Earth. Or so she told him, as well as the exact location where these physical remains could be found. After a little digging Hubert did indeed discover an ancient skeleton at that exact spot. Once and for all confirming that it hadn't all just been a hallucination, as his buddies kept insisting.<br /> Hubert went from the hole he dug right to the local dealer's door. He wanted to talk to Kornelia again, so he'd need to buy more pigment. Not something the guy normally carried; it would cost a pretty pfennig. Yet a week later the young man was once again snorting black powder. Kornelia seemed overjoyed to meet him again, requesting he rebury her skeletal remains in consecrated ground, setting her soul free. Hubert however declined, requiring something from the restless spirit first; hidden treasure. Hubert was a school dropout with no prospects, he had to get money somehow. A pet ghost seemed like the answer. Kornelia had been invisibly floating around for hundreds of years, she ought to know where he'd find riches.<br /> Lacking someone to tell him he might have watched too many children's adventure films, Hubert kept pressuring Kornelia. And of course he had to keep doing pigment to urge her on. At least that's what he told himself, as the youngster sank deeper in debt with his dealer. Finally coming to a point where the crook couldn't take anymore of the lies, the promises of a big payday right around the corner. In a fit of anger the pigment pusher kicked Hubert's face in, not stopping until it was a lifeless pulp.<br /> Hubert was Reaped by a familiar face; his long deceased grandfather. He told the Enfant to run and never look back. The local wraiths were already hunting for him, Kornelia was out for vengeance. Hubert's flight ended in Necropolis Berlin, hoping to disappear among the hundreds of thousands other wraiths that dwelt there. His ambitions eventually led this hue to finding a new home with NextWorld.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Image:</b> Hubert literally looks like a ghost, an entirely translucent apparition. A tall, thin man who appears to be about twenty. With short cropped hair and a ring through his right earlobe. He's wearing the tracksuit and filthy sneakers he died in. When on missions Hubert usually has an Artifact rifle slung over his shoulder.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> On the surface you appear to be a brash young man who's quite full of himself. In truth you never liked yourself much. In life the solution was to numb those unpleasant emotions, until an opportunity would present itself to escape your white thrash roots. Fortunately in death you've become a bit more realistic, understanding the worth of hard work. You're quite motivated as a NextWorld employee, the ticket to becoming a big man in the Underworld. And yet, another part of you just wants to do nothing but Skinride pigment addicts.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Rogue<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Competitor<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 1, Athletics 1, Awareness , Brawl 2, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Drive 1, Firearms 2, Larceny 1, Leadership 1, Melee 2, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Enigmas 1, Technology 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 1, Artifact 4, Contacts 1, Eidolon 2, Haunt 3, Memoriam 2, Notoriety 1, Relic , Status 1<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Puppetry 3, Usury 2<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Become wealthy (Pride) 4, Get high on pigment (Self-Hatred) 4, Protect loved ones (Love) 2<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Drug Dealer 3, Kornelia's Skeleton 3, Napoleonic War Memorial 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Pathos:</b> 7<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 9<br /> <b>Shadow:</b> The Quiescent<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 4<br /> <b>Thorns:</b> Freudian Slip, Nightmares<br /> <b>Dark Passions:</b> Become wealthy (Envy) 4, Get high on pigment (Self-Hatred) 4, Protect loved ones (Lust) 2</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 06-25-2022, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T04:39:26-07:00","id":1487566,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>8. Johanna Kessler, Angel of the Forge</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A Silent bureaucrat of the Leipzig Necropolis, where all Thralls know to fear the Angel. It's she who decides which souls are fit for work and who should instead serve the Necropolis as raw materials. As the Hierarch who selects souls for the forges Johanna can scarcely leave the safety of the Citadel. Though the current situation is nothing compared to what would happen if her wartime crimes became widely known.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Johanna was born at the dawn of the 20th century, her father a doctor coming from a long line of Leipzig physicians. As a young woman she continued the family tradition by marrying a medical student; the future doctor Herbert Kessler. Like many German doctors at the time, Johanna's husband was a proponent of eugenics and what the Nazis called &quot;racial hygi\u00ebne&quot;. This ideology led the couple down a dark path. Once the Second World War started Hitler's regime wanted to unburden itself from those people they labelled &quot;life unworthy of life&quot;. Dr. Kessler was recruited to assist with the T4 extermination program at Leipzig-D\u00f6sen Sanatorium, Johanna chose to join him as a nurse. The woman was put to work in the disabled children's wing. Where the intention was no longer to care for the patients, but to hasten their deaths. Johanna had great difficulty functioning there at first. With her marriage remaining barren she'd always enjoyed the presence of children. Yet pressured by Herbert and the nursing staff she swiftly learned to dehumanize her charges, fulfilling her vile duty to the German state. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In 1941 her husband was invited to lend his expertise in occupied Poland, Johanna would stay behind, continue her work at the D\u00f6sen facility. From then on she would see little of Herbert, he only rarely returned home. There were regular letters though, until in the autumn of 1943 their correspondence suddenly fell silent. He was killed in the line of duty, Johanna was never given any specifics. From that point her service to the German people was the only thing that gave life meaning. Even after the last children were gone the widow kept nursing at the same institution, right up to the spring of 1945.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Johanna had always refused to believe Germany could lose the war. However when American troops steamrolled into the city that illusion was finally shattered, all was lost. The nurse knew which poison to inject herself with for a quick death, she had murdered plenty of children in such a manner. Her passing was not as painless as she'd expected though, she left the Skinlands in agony.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">During the Maelstrom plagued mid-1940s the Leipzig Necropolis adopted a policy in which all suicides were automatically sent to the forges. Fortunately for Johanna the local Hierarchs tended to make an exception for those cornered Nazis that'd taken their own life. Courtesy of a shadowy Circle, that was to become the Nebula Group, exercising their influence to save loyal party members. When the dust finally settled Johanna was among friends in the Silent Legion, many National Socialists had died in despair. She owes everything to their continued support, with time rising to the rank of Minister.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Image: </b>A plump woman wearing a WW2 era German nurses' uniform; a striped blue dress under a white apron. Over Johanna's blond hair a cap is tied. This cap, an armband and her broche are all adorned with a red cross. She appears to be in her 40s. Although normally of her features only the wraith's gray eyes are visible. The rest is covered behind a mask of black soulsteel, forged to resemble a pair of bird wings.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints: </b>Your personality doesn't seem all that pronounced. Sociable, yet lacking any warmth. Respectful to even the lowest of Thralls, never showing them any real compassion though.<br /> Ideology continues to be your bulwark against self-hatred. You're not a monster, the Hierarchy justifies the terrible role you fulfill in the Underworld, just like Nazism did the same for you among the Quick. And yet you regularly bend and break Stygian policy. Many wraiths are condemned to the forges, not for their spiritual weakness, but because you don't consider them to be good Germans.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Follower<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Pragmatist<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 2, Manipulation 4, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 4, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 2, Awareness 3, Empathy 1, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Drive 1, Etiquette 3, Larceny 1, Leadership 2<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Bureaucracy 3, Enigmas 1, Medicine 2, Politics 1, Science 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 3, Artifact 1, Contacts 2, Eidolon 2, Mentor 1, Notoriety 3, Status 4<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Castigate 2, Fatalism 1, Intimation 2, Lifeweb 1<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Further the Nazi cause (Duty) 4, Discover what happened to husband (Love) 4, Be a model Hierarch (Pride) 2<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> D\u00f6sen Sanatorium Building 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Pathos:</b> 5<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 10<br /> <b>Shadow: </b>The Director<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 4<br /> <b>Thorns:</b> Dark Allies, Nightmares, Spectre Prestige, Whispers<br /> <b>Dark Passions:</b> Corrupt or destroy innocent souls (Envy) 4, Surrender to the D\u00f6sen Striplings (Self-Hatred) 3</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 07-23-2022, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T05:33:01-07:00","id":1491288,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>9. Shanar Baran, back alley projector</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A young refugee of Kurdish extraction who's hooked on pigment, letting her see ghosts and project into the Underworld. She's become a street medium, when Leipzig's poor or homeless have a problem of a ghostly nature; they know Shanar's the person to contact.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Shanar grew up on a small farm in Syrian Kurdistan. Where she enjoyed a carefree childhood of herding sheep and picking tomatoes. During her teens came the Syrian Civil War, allowing the Kurdish state of Rojava to form. The girl believed this to be the dawn of a better tomorrow. Hopes that were utterly crushed when an ISIS militia attacked their home. The terrorists shot her father in cold blood, taking the farm, Shanar and her mother included, for themselves. For weeks they lived the life of heavily veiled slaves, until the night her mother helped the girl slip away. She fled north, eventually crossing the border into Turkey.<br /> Once in Turkey only fellow Kurds showed any interest in her plight. The refugee accepted an offer, by PKK fighters, of employment on a farm in the East of the country. Tending a crop unlike any she'd been familiar with, while armed guards kept the area secure. This did not bother her, it was the painful memories that made life nearly impossible. The image of her father's corpse, her mother's cries in the night. One of the other girls working the fields noticed her pain, offering a solution. Shanar was introduced to what became of the plants they'd been growing; a black powder known in the West as pigment. Snorting the substance did indeed do wonders, easing her suffering for a few hours. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The other girl had warned her that first time; go easy on the stuff, workers weren't supposed to touch the drug. She paid this warning little heed, pigment became a habit. Even though it caused her to see gruesome monsters roaming the farm, the drug was the only thing that made life livable. One midday break, while she was once again getting high, her father appeared. He warned that they were coming, she was to be shot for stealing their product. Immediately Shanar started running, escaping into the wilderness. As Turkey would no longer be safe, she followed the refugee trail into Europe. Weeks later the young woman arrived in Leipzig, where she received asylum. Once settled the young woman started experimenting with the effects of pigment in earnest. Eventually ending up on the streets, as heavy use of an illegal drug forced Shanar to live off the grid.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Image:</b> A woman with dusky skin and dark eyes, 22 years of age. Regardless of her youth, to Western eyes she dresses like a grandmother. Long dresses, castoffs donated to charity, multiple sizes too large for her wiry frame. A red on black floral shawl, rests on Shanar's shoulders, hanging halfway down the back. For practical reasons the girl keeps her hair fairly short. The result is a spiky mop, ebony in color.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Roleplaying Tips: </b>You don't get high anymore, you no longer take pigment to dull your trauma. Rather you do so in order to reconnect with your deceased father. Him appearing to you, in Turkey, shook your worldview. Islam does not have all the answers when it comes to death and the afterlife. Giving you a great need to discover what this means for your soul and those of your loved ones.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\ufeffEverything you've been through has left your compassionate side intact though. You truly care for people, always willing to help out. Also because you see everything as a new learning opportunity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nature:</b> Scientist</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Demeanor:</b> Caregiver<br /> <b>Physical: </b>Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social: </b>Charisma 3, Manipulation 2, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Mental: </b>Perception 3, Intelligence 3, Wits 4<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 1, Athletics 1, Awareness 2, Empathy 2, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Etiquette 1, Larceny 1, Meditation 3, Melee 1, Stealth 3<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Enigmas 1, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Occult 3<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 2, Contacts 3, Fame 1, Notoriety 1<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Argos 2, Embody 1, Fatalism 1, Lifeweb 1, Puppetry 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Passions:</b> Reconnect with family (Love) 3, Learn about the afterlife (Worry) 2<br /> <b>Tethers:</b> Body 5, Photo of Home 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Pathos:</b> 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Merits:</b> Language (Arabic, German + mother tongue Kurdish)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Flaw:</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Addiction (Pigment), PTSD</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 09-19-2022, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T01:50:45-08:00","id":1498514,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>10. Jella Fuchs, a ghost haunted</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This relatively young wraith is one of NextWorld's earliest Shadowlands hires. In their employ she skulks around in the offices and boardrooms of Germany or further afield. Though in recent years she does so while constantly looking over her shoulder.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Born and raised in Leipzig, Jella came of age in the era that brought capitalism to Eastern Germany. Many in Jella's life chose to seize this opportunity, her father for instance started a restaurant. While the young woman herself joined her fianc\u00e9e's new business; installing industrial machinery. Ben Fuchs managed the technical side of the company, while she put her accounting degree to good use. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The newlyweds had a couple of prosperous years, after which the economic situation turned against them. The stress of their failing business had her husband turn abusive, seemingly blaming her for their imminent bankruptcy. Ben didn't even show up for the funeral of his own mother-in-law, who'd died of cancer. For Jella this was the final straw, she filed for divorce. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In the coming months Ben kept stalking Jella. Managing to instill a massive guilt about what happened to their enterprise and also about she leaving at such a time. That guilt is how he manipulated her to get into his car that fatal day. They were supposed to look over a financial plan to help restart his business, instead Jella was treated to yet another plea for her to return to him. She once again refused, to which Ben responded by driving straight into a canal.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jella was killed on impact, while her former husband was pulled from the water and resuscitated. Without proof to the contrary Ben's attempted suicide, successful murder, was ruled an accident. He left the hospital a free man, but in a wheelchair. Ben would never walk again, cursing Jella's name for his misfortune.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Meanwhile in the Shadowlands his ex-wife was consumed by remorse, rejecting the Dictum Mortuum in a bid to financially support him. When NextWorld first opened its Berlin offices Jella was the first ghost they recruited. Her knowledge of accountancy made her uniquely suited to corporate espionage. With her generous wages all being deposited in Ben's bank account. It made no difference to the man though, remaining just as bitter. He drank and gambled all the money away without even wondering where it came from. Which had Jella surmise Ben needed a new purpose in life instead, a chance to earn his own salary once more. Her own projection firm would not hire a living man with her ex's profile, Orpheus Group might though. Jella called in a favor and soon Ben was installing cryogenic cradles in Orpheus' German facility. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A year later Jella's troubles began in earnest. The wraith's ex-husband appeared before her, kicking and punching her straight into a Harrowing. It would appear Ben had developed into a talented Skimmer, seeking vengeance against the woman he deems to have ruined his life. Yella has been mercilessly pursued by him ever since. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Image: </b>A woman of around 30 with intelligent green eyes, part of a determined face. Her Corpus appears clad in business attire, consisting of a red blouse, black skirt and pumps. Jella's blond hair is tied together in a ponytail.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> Outwardly you come across as the consummate professional. When you're on the job every word or action has a clear purpose. Only a hint that Ben might be near can visibly affect your cool. Rationally you know different, yet you can't help but feel everything your husband accuses you of is true. You loved him, you broke him, fixing Ben's life should be your main goal in this afterlife.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Penitent<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Pragmatist<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 4, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 1, Athletics 1, Brawl 1, Empathy 1, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Crafts 1, Drive 1, Etiquette 2, Larceny 1, Melee 1, Stealth 2<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Bureaucracy 2, Computer 2, Enigmas 2, Finance 2, Investigation 1, Science 1, Technology 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 1, Contacts 3, Eidolon 1, Haunt 3, Memoriam 2, Notoriety 1, Status 2<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Inhabit 4, Puppetry 1, Usury 2<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Placate ex-husband (Guilt) 4, Protect family members (Love) 3, Prove capabilities (Pride) 3<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Father 2, Fuchs Maschineninstallation former offices 2, Ex-husband 5, Karl Heine Canal 1<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Pathos:</b> 7<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 9<br /> <b>Shadow:</b> The Abuser<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 5<br /> <b>Thorns:</b> Dark Allies, Honeyed Tongue, Nightmares, Trick of the Light,<br /> <b>Dark Passions:</b> Corrupt romantic relationships (Envy) 2, Let ex-husband destroy me (Self-Hatred) 5</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T04:39:53-08:00","id":1499053,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>11. Robert Feinnes</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">One of hundreds of British soldiers that lost his life when in December 1944 a V2 rocket struck the Rex movie theater. He's one of the Plainsmen, a Circle that roams Antwerp's outskirts south of the Necropolis' walls. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In life Robert was a farmer's son that grew up in the Kentish countryside. A patriotic young man that enlisted as soon as the UK declared war on Nazi Germany. He didn't see any action however until well after D-Day, fighting his way up through France as part of an infantry unit. Eventually ending up in the city where an afternoon showing of a western film would cost him his life.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">After being Reaped Robert was sent directly to Stygia, where the Enfant was inducted into the Grim military. After the 5<sup>th</sup> Great Maelstrom erupted he took part in some of the most intense combat the Underworld had ever seen, removing Robert's appetite for warfare once and for all. Fortunately he was rewarded for his service with a quiet posting near his former home. Which lasted until the last of his Fetters there had died. Subsequently Robert returned to Antwerp, where his final link to the Shadowlands lay buried. However, he chose to leave active service in his Legion in favor of joining the Plainsmen. Robert now attempts to walk a path of pacificism. Often leading to conflict with his Circle-mates and the harsh realities of afterlife on the frontier. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Image:</b> Paranoid about being pressed into active service again, Robert often changes his appearance. Though he never manages to remove the thousand-yard-stare from his eyes. Also his looks follow the general theme of a handsome man in his prime, wearing unassuming mid-20<sup>th</sup> century garb.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints: </b>You've faced hell and its Spectral hordes, now you'll do everything in your power to never return there. Transcendence you consider the only sure way to remain safe indefinitely. You're still far from enlightenment though, mostly you're just frightened. Which you mostly manage to hide from your compatriots under a mild mannered exterior, having a talent for steering your Circle away from trouble.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Rogue<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Mediator<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 3, Manipulation 4, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 1, Athletics 1, Awareness 1, Brawl 2, Empathy 1, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Crafts 2, Drive 2, Etiquette 1, Firearms 3, Meditation 1, Melee 2, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Bureaucracy 1, Enigmas 1, Medicine 1, Occult 2<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 2, Contacts 4, Eidolon 3, Notoriety 1, Status 1<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Castigate 2, Moliate 2, Outrage 3<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Achieve Transcendence (Hope) 3, Avoid the forces of Oblivion (Fear) 4, Have physical remains buried in home soil (Love) 1<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Physical Remains 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Pathos:</b> 5<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Shadow:</b> The Monster<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 3<br /> <b>Thorns:</b> Dark Allies, Nightmares, Shadow Call<br /> <b>Dark Passions:</b> Commit acts of violence (Bloodlust) 5, Desecrate burial sites of other ghosts (Jealousy) 3</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T20:43:41-07:00","id":1517624,"title":"","content":"<b>12. Juanita Reyes, the vengeful mother</b><br /> A Doppelganger who's been able to reconnect with her now adult son, a result of his pigment habit. She's urging him to seek revenge against those who abused and killed her.<br /> Like many generations of Reyes' before her she was born in the shadow of Don Teofil Bratovitch's hacienda. Even though they were in mid-20<sup>th</sup> century Mexico, for all intents and purposes her family were serfs, part of the estate. From a young age Juanita cleaned up after the Bratovitches, a firsthand witness to their wickedness. The girl had no intention of bringing a child into such brutal circumstances. Unfortunately the master's abuses took away her choice in the matter. She birthed a boy, named Eduardo after his grandfather. To add insult to injury; that little boy would be orphaned only a few years later. Juanita had been unable to wash a bloodstain out of Sonia Bratovitch's dress, who in response strangled the servant.<br /> Juanita was Reaped by a tight-knit Circle of the hacienda's wraiths. Like her they'd all suffered under the Bratovitches in life. She followed their example by dedicating her afterlife to watching over her loved ones, be a guardian angel to little Eduardo. It was hard to look on as that innocent child was gradually corrupted by his masters, becoming a ruthless gangster. It gave Juanita's Shadow plenty of ammunition, Spectrehood was the eventual result.<br /> When a deal was struck between Don Teofil and Consuela DelaCruz, one of the pigment barons, Spectres started to descend on the hacienda en masse. The local wraiths did their best to fight them off, unfortunately they had a traitor in their midst. Juanita's Shadow-Eaten condition had remained undetected, she was perfectly placed to undermine their defense. Through the Doppelganger's efforts the hacienda's ghosts were picked off one by one, until only Juanita remained.<br /> The Spectres who laid claim, to what was to become a pigment farm, told Juanita stories of Grandmother's glory. She became an eager convert to the cause, totally surrendering her Corpus and mind to this greater power. She remembers little from the period that followed, a blur of violent gore among the Kakos stromithicarum plants, fulfilling Grandmother's will. After a while though she kept seeing flashes of her son's face, momentarily returning the Spectre's sense of self. Over time these occurrences pulled Juanita out of her daze entirely, realizing there were more ways than one to serve Grandmother.<br /> From across the Shroud Juanita found Eduardo easily approachable when he was high, which was most of the time. Once convinced she wasn't just a hallucination her son was easily turned against the Bratovitches. It's why he's now driving a stolen truckload of pigment toward Juarez, to vengeance. Mother knows best and she says Sonia Bratovitch needs to die first.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A brown-skinned girl in her late teens, with black curls down to her shoulders. She's seen wearing a knee-length white dress and walking barefoot. Juanita's Corpus shows obvious signs of strangulation; bloodshot eyes, a blueish face and her neck nearly black with bruising. This Spectre is always accompanied by the smell of both blood and soap.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You come across as a sweet woman, a loving parent. Though your cheerfulness is obviously an act, your anguish cannot be hidden. The way you've lost everything to the Bratovitches has made you hate existence itself. It's why in your total misery you're devoted to Grandmother, soon she will devour everything. Unfortunately soon isn't enough anymore, you're determined to see Eduardo converted to the cause. He'll stand next you when Grandmother finally claims you both. And you'll also make sure all the Bratovitches are long gone by then.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Conniver<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Caregiver<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 1<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 2, Manipulation 3, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 1, Athletics 1, Awareness 1, Brawl 1, Empathy 2, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Crafts 1, Etiquette 1, Meditation 1, Melee 1, Performance (Singing) 2, Stealth 2<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Enigmas 1, Medicine 1, Occult 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 1, Contacts 1, Memoriam 1, Shadowlands 3, Status 2<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Argos 2, Collogue 1, Keening 2, Outrage 1, Shroud Rending 1<br /> <b>Dark Passions:</b> Drag family into Oblivion (Twisted Love) 3, Destroy the Bratovitches (Hate) 5<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Son 2, Sonia Bratovitch 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 5<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 6\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 07-28-2023, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T10:45:29-08:00","id":1527504,"title":"","content":"Written for a VtM Sabbat game, but steeped in Orpheus lore:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>13. Miguel Amaral, Caribbean pigment baron</b><br /> The man who controls the pigment smuggling routes between Colombia, Mexico and the US East Coast. Not as powerful as Consuela DelaCruz or Federico Peralto, he doesn't have any plantations himself, yet instrumental to both their operations. Though earlier in life Don Miguel belonged to several Project Twilight agencies. One of these taught him to project into the Underworld, becoming a skimmer.<br /> As a boy he grew up as part of the Cuban establishment. The Amarals were true believers in the Revolution, Miguel was no different. A result of his father fighting alongside Castro and Guevara. Footsteps the young man followed in when during the early 1980s he started his own military career. Which was nearly cut short when his entire unit was slaughtered during a jungle training exercise. A reanimated corpse, which seemed impervious to bullets, butchered all of his men. Only Miguel survived by finally destroying the monster with a hand grenade.<br /> This unbelievable disaster wasn't the end, as he'd feared, of the young officer. Instead of a dishonorable discharge, or court martial, he was transferred to an unnamed division of the Military Counterintelligence Directorate. There Miguel soon learned that each soldier there had survived an encounter with the undead like he had. They were to put these terrifying experiences to good use for the protection of the Cuban people and the Revolution. Over the next few years Miguel led missions throughout his own nation, but also abroad in Angola and Nicaragua. When it came to combatting the supernatural Sergeant Amaral's service record grew so impressive that his file eventually ended up on a Russian desk.<br /> The GRU, Soviet Military Intelligence, wished to recruit this Cuban officer for Project Zmei. This was an effort to create psychic agents out of soldiers. They were hoping a man like Sergeant Amaral could more easily bridge the gap between the supernatural and the military, cause the project had only seen limited success so far. After spending years undergoing instruction in biofeedback and mental conditioning Miguel did indeed develop the ability to project his soul into the Underworld. Though by that time the Soviet Union was dissolving and the general leading Project Zmei had deserted to parts unknown.<br /> During the 1990s Miguel decided to strike out on his own as well. In the previous decade he'd befriended Nicaraguan military officers who were now growing rich in the cocaine trade. He accepted the offer to join their operation. Over the next years Amaral became just as wealthy, though playing a game he found increasingly hard to survive in. Hence why a couple of years ago, when pigment first gained popularity, he saw an opportunity to get in on the ground floor of a market not yet dominated by the cartels. Don Miguel has since been doing quite well, as a skimmer having the advantage of understanding the drug's true nature far better than most in his business. The proliferation of the Death Merchants, and other incorporeal sicarios, hasn't caught him by surprise. Amaral's Yucat\u00e1n hacienda is well guarded against such assassins.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A middle-aged Latino who's just below average height. Though Miguel shows his years he does appear to have kept himself fairly fit. That's in part an illusion however, which he maintains thanks to his well tailored suits. These usually have a light color scheme and are worn sans tie. Amaral still has a military haircut, a contrast with the man's bushy moustache.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> A softspoken gentleman who gives concise orders. Though sociable you're someone who likes to keep a low profile. The true reason you built this criminal empire isn't personal pride, it's a private rivalry with your long deceased father. Like the elder Amaral you tried to be successful as a communist, yet discovered you're far more talented at capitalism. Though never cruel you have little issue ordering someone's death, or even getting your own hands dirty. It helps that you care little for what others think of you, besides your late father that is.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Competitor<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Director<br /> <b>Apparent Age:</b> around 50<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 3, Manipulation 4, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 4, Intelligence 3, Wits 4<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 4, Athletics 1, Awareness 3, Brawl 2, Empathy 1, Intimidation 2, Leadership 3, Streetwise 4, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Drive 2, Etiquette 2, Firearms 4, Melee 2, Stealth 2, Survival 2<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Finance 2, Investigation 2, Law 1, Medicine 1, Occult 3, Politics 2, Technology 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 5, Armory 4, Base of Operation 5, Contacts 5, Influence 3, Legacy 2, Memoriam 2, Paranormal Tools 3, Resources 6, Retainers 5<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Argos 1, Embody 1, Lifeweb 1, Outrage 2<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Care for loved ones 3, Outdo father's legacy 2<br /> <b>Tethers:</b> Body 5, Son 3, Wife 2<br /> <b>Virtues:</b> Conscience 2, Self-Control 4, Courage 4<br /> <b>Morality:</b> Humanity 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Pathos: </b>6<br /> <b>Merits/Flaws:</b> Language (English, Russian + mother tongue Spanish)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T17:58:34-08:00","id":1527646,"title":"","content":"<b>14. Yenifer Del Toro, the Juarez Ghostwatcher</b><br /> An adolescent who recently received the distinct honor of being one of the youngest people to ever be named an Associate of the Arcanum. Warranted by her detailed, and ongoing, study of ghostly society in Ciudad Ju\u00e1rez. As of yet no Arcanist has met her in the flesh, otherwise they'd likely be horrified to learn how Yenifer achieves these spectacular insights.<br /> Though she went to Catholic school Yenifer didn't believe in the supernatural for most of her youth. She remained an extraordinarily rationale kid until her mid teens. That's when she witnessed a fellow student being accosted by a poltergeist, in full view of half the school. The nuns and Padre Gustavo, their headmaster, looked on just as helplessly as everyone else. Which in Yenifer's mind clearly demonstrated that the Church didn't have the answers either. The girl was determined to get to the bottom of this phenomena though, hence why she became a student of the occult.<br /> In the following months Yenifer gained a rudimentary knowledge of the paranormal through library books. However it was her Internet searches that allowed the girl to dig deeper. In the message boards and chatrooms frequented by fellow occult geeks she first learned of the Arcanum and pigment. Both the elite scholarly organisation studying the supernatural, and the new drug supposedly allowing one to see ghosts, fascinated Yenifer immensely. The Arcanum was still out of reach, but the teen had no problem finding black heroin on Juarez's streets. At first she found buying and using the narcotic incredibly scary. But Yenifer kept at it, cause while under the influence she really was perceiving ghosts.<br /> Keeping a drug habit secret from her parents wasn't easy though. Her school results hadn't started to suffer yet, but money became an issue. Pigment didn't come cheap, the girl quickly burned through her savings. The teenage occultist was already cataloguing all she witnessed while high, a research project she definitely didn't want to abandon. And by that time she was of course also already hopelessly addicted. Yenifer ended up solving her financial woes with their cause; she was to be her school's first pigment dealer. Selling just about enough, at inflated prices, to cover her own usage.<br /> By some miracle Yenifer never got caught and was able to keep her grades up, she made it to graduation. Pressured by her father to follow in his footsteps the teen has recently begun studying medicine at the Juarez university. Her parents were generous enough to rent her an apartment close to campus. Yenifer has since made good use of the view. She's now permanently under the influence, obsessively typing out everything the nearby restless dead are up to. These reports are regularly mailed to the Arcanum Chapter House in Mexico City. She doesn't go to her classes anymore, or really outside much at all. This teen pigment dealer's supplier comes to her. Same with her customers, who she sometimes requests to bring food. Spectres also visit regularly, assuring Yenifer they'll do all in their power to keep her business and her research going.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A young Latina who's sickly looking, the girl's pale and weighs too little for her above average height. Yenifer's black hair is usually greasy and unkempt, unless she's expected to meet family. Who also get to see her in other attire than the black tracksuit she spends most of her time in. Whatever she wears it's always long-sleeved though, as to cover the tracks on her arms.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> The people you meet never get your full attention, instead your eyes always seem to follow something past them. Unless they can further your studies into the paranormal you also brush off everyone as soon as possible. After having used pigment for so long you don't come across as high though. You're an absolute wreck without the narcotic, but function relatively normal when under its influence. More alarmingly you seem to completely lack a danger sense. Because of how lucky you've been so far you have a detached way of looking at both the criminal underworld and the supernatural, not acknowledging their potential lethality.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Architect<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Deviant<br /> <b>Apparent Age:</b> 18<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 1<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 3, Intelligence 4, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 3, Awareness 1, Brawl 1, Expression 1, Intimidation 1, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Etiquette 2, Larceny 1, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 2, Computer 2, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Occult (Ghosts) 3, Politics (Ghosts) 1, Science 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 2, Base of Operation 2, Contacts 3, Mentor 1, Paranormal Tools 1, Resources 2<br /> <b>Virtues:</b> Conscience 4, Self-Control 1, Courage 4<br /> <b>Morality:</b> Humanity 7<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 3<br /> <b>Merits/Flaws:</b> Addiction (Pigment), Language (English, Latin + mother tongue Spanish)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 01-14-2024, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T15:43:48-08:00","id":1531038,"title":"","content":"Finally an actual wraith again, but still more of a crossover character:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>15. Klaus von Braun, Nazi occultist wraith</b><br /> A now deceased former Thule Society member, who through his grandchild is leading a skinhead motorcycle gang. Through them he hopes to fulfill a 60-year-old obsession; locating the obsidian sarcophagus.<br /> Klaus grew up in Berlin during Germany's tumultuous 1920s and 30s. Though belonging to a family of academics, moneyed and of noble descent, meant the boy was mostly insulated from these troubles. Not entirely though, cause like so many other Germans the von Brauns got caught up in nationalistic fervor. Klaus' father had already been a member of the Thule Society since the Great War's end. When his occult fraternity chose to back Hitler's rise to power this spineless scholar followed suit.<br /> And like father like son. After earning an ancient history degree, at Leipzig University, young Klaus joined the Society as well. By then certain figures within the regime, those aware of the supernatural, had extended their iron grip over Germany to the Thule Gesellschaft. Like the military they were to build up their strength, in preparation for the upcoming war. For Klaus that meant he was to study Hedge Magic, as to become a skilled field occultist.<br /> Klaus' first official assignment was in the summer of 1940, within weeks of France's fall. He was sent to Paris, where under the command of Alfred Rosenberg he'd assist in the looting of mystic treasures. Though the young Nazi was indoctrinated enough to have no issue with ransacking the belongings of Jewish families, he was instead allocated a research function. Making use of his university degree, and sorcerous ability, Klaus pored over historical archives and museum collections, in search of supernaturally potent artifacts. It's while studying an archeology paper he first learned of an object that had no name, only a description; that of &quot;obsidian sarcophagus&quot;.<br /> The artifact had been discovered in the early 1920s, during a French excavation of ancient Carthage. It was transported back to Paris, where it was extensively studied and yet nothing of substance could be ascertained. However, where French academia failed Klaus was able to succeed. An occult tome, 'acquired' by the Thule Society, shed light on the mysterious sarcophagus. The text spoke of a secret demon war fought alongside the siege of Carthage. The archeological find matched the description of a powerful supernatural relic with which the Romans supposedly defeated the city.<br /> Klaus was sure he found the key to a swift Axis victory. Unfortunately for him the obsidian sarcophagus hadn't been seen since 1923. The Thule sorcerer had no choice but to continue performing his duties as before, hoping that in the process the artifact's current location would be revealed. As the years went on all the useful relics he did track down earned him a medal. Klaus cared little for this though, he remained obsessed with the sarcophagus.<br /> And then finally von Braun came across documentation which revealed it had been shipped across the Atlantic, to Mexico. The dire state on the Eastern Front helped convince his superiors he should travel in pursuit of this suspected wonder weapon. Hence why in the spring of 1944 the young occultist could trade in occupied France for the state of Chihuahua. The Nazi, under the assumed identity of a Swiss archeologist, spent the war's final year chasing down clues, throughout northern Mexico, about the artifact's exact location. Until the day he learnt of Germany's capitulation Klaus kept believing he could personally turn the tide, they just needed the sarcophagus' power.<br /> Unfortunately the young man didn't stop being a Nazi with the death of Hitler. In the post-war era Klaus remained preoccupied with what could be salvaged from the Thule Society and the Third Reich at large. Yet most of his old associates could only be reconnected with through necromantic means, if at all. If von Braun wanted to make a difference he'd have to build up his own powerbase. When the Cold War begun he saw an opportunity to do just that; the Americans were in the market for German expertise. Though Klaus soon found out this didn't include the mystical.<br /> That changed in 1952, with the creation of the FBI's Special Affairs Department. Being recruited by them as an occult consultant was his ticket out of Mexico, into the United States. Though this was still in pursuit of his white whale; that polished black rock. Klaus made himself useful to the federal agents, gradually getting into a position where he could ask favors in return. The intelligence SAD helped him gather pointed toward the obsidian sarcophagus being hidden in the southern US, near the Mexican border. So that's where the von Brauns, their name since changed to Brown, ended up settling.<br /> He remained on call for the SAD until well into the 1980s. When he finally retired the old man felt he had accomplished nothing, a life wasted. It's why he finally started to show interest in his grandson, young Heinrich. Klaus had never been much of a family man, but considered the impressionable kid perfect to continue his quest. By the time the von Braun patriarch was losing his battle with lung cancer 'Rich' had been fully indoctrinated. A neo-Nazi skinhead, and sorcerer, just as determined to locate the obsidian sarcophagus.<br /> The dying man knew exactly what awaited him after death, neither the heaven he hoped for nor the hell he deserved. After escaping his Caul the Enfant immediately sought contact with the Nebula Group, an underground Nazi Circle he'd long since been aware of. To his dismay Klaus discovered that those who lived to a ripe old age were accorded little respect, not having died for the cause. That he spent the war's closing year safely in Mexico, with nothing to show for it, didn't endear him to any Nebula wraiths either. They made clear no one in the organisation would risk their Corpus for von Braun, he's on his own in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <b>Image: </b>A decrepit eighty-year-old who resembles little more than wrinkly skin loosely draped over bone. This frail wretch is unclothed except for a hospital gown, he hasn't been able to afford any Moliation yet. Klaus' wizened face is dominated by intelligent eyes, gray in color. His presence is always accompanied by the stale smell of old tobacco.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints: </b>You behave like a socially awkward nerd. So fearful of the Underworld that you hardly leave Heinrich 'Rich' Brown's, the grandson you're skinriding, body's safety. Though beneath that pathetic exterior there's still a ruthless Nazi who wishes to be respected, who needs to change the world. Until the obsidian sarcophagus has been secured you consider your entire existence a complete failure. Though that hasn't lead you to examine your own choices and beliefs. It's everyone else who's failed you, and continue to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Activist<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Martyr<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 1, Stamina 1<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 1, Manipulation 4, Appearance 1<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 2, Intelligence 4, Wits 4<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 1, Awareness 2, Empathy 1, Expression 1, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Drive 2, Etiquette 3, Firearms 2, Leadership 1, Meditation 2, Melee (Fencing) 2, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics (History) 3, Bureaucracy 1, Enigmas 3, Investigation 1, Occult (Artifacts) 4, Politics 1, Science 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Contacts 3, Eidolon 2, Memoriam 2, Notoriety 1<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Argos 1, Puppetry 2, Usury 3<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Bring about a Fourth Reich (Duty) 1, Earn Nebula Group's respect (Pride) 2, Mold grandson into copy of oneself (Vanity) 2, Secure the obsidian sarcophagus (Obsession) 5<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Grandson 2, Nazi Medal 3, Personal Journal 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Pathos:</b> 7<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 10<br /> <b>Shadow:</b> The Perfectionist<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 5<br /> <b>Thorns:</b> Aura of Corruption, Bad Luck, Tainted Touch<br /> <b>Dark Passions:</b> Descend into Oblivion (Self-Hatred) 1, Destroy family (Shame) 2, Destroy obsidian sarcophagus (Frustration) 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 03-23-2024, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T14:13:51-07:00","id":1558899,"title":"","content":"<b>16. Reut Cohen, the dybbuk whisperer</b><br /> A young woman belonging to the Hasidic Jewish community of Mexico City. As a result of her medium gift she's been contacted by an ancestor, a man murdered in the Holocaust. Under his direction she's now determined to oppose the Nazi occult.<br /> Reut was the first child born to a conservative family residing in Mexico City's old Jewish hub of La Merced. A neighborhood where the Cohens had settled, after fleeing Nazi Germany, during the 1930s. In the post-war era they were immensely grateful for having escaped the horrors in Europe, growing only more religious as a consequence. Hence Reut arriving in an extremely devout household when born in 1980.<br /> The first two decades of the girl's life were quiet and uneventful. She simply did what was expected of her, being taught how to become the perfect Hasidic wife and mother. But then suddenly Reut's predictable path towards marriage was upended when she started seeing things. The young woman watched the spirits of the dead walking the Mexico City streets. Reut immediately realized she wasn't going crazy. These were the dybbuks of Jewish folklore.<br /> For months the young woman didn't know what to do with her supernatural sight, considering it a curse she wished to keep secret. But then one of these ghosts showed up in her bedroom, introducing himself as Aaron. The dybbuk told her he was family, a great-uncle who'd remained in Europe and murdered by the Nazis. In life Aaron had been a member of the Arcanum, attached to their Chapter House in Paris. There he was studying a tome describing a secret demon war fought alongside the siege of Carthage. When the French Cohens were sent to their deaths, the text went to Klaus von Braun. He was a Thule Society researcher, the reason Aaron's soul was to remain restless into the 21st century. The then recently deceased Nazi occultist's ghost was still out there as well, determined to use knowledge gained, from that stolen tome, to unleash a great evil upon the world. Aaron convinced Reut she'd received her gift from G*d to aid him in stopping von Braun.<br /> However, Reut's sheltered upbringing had in no way prepared her for such a divine mission. Determined as she may be, the young woman has so far heavily relied on great-uncle Aaron's guidance. This is how she first came into contact with the Arcanum. At her dybbuk relative's urging Reut simply showed up on the doorstep of their Mexico City Chapter House. The resident Arcanists turned out to be most interested in meeting a direct link to one of their secret society's late members. Though unwilling to become directly involved in the Cohen duo's quest, the Chapter House's head agreed to an exchange of information. An arrangement the Arcanum formalized by granting Reut the rank of Associate.<br /> Through Arcanist aid, and interviewing a great many dybbuks, the two Cohens have since figured out what Klaus von Braun had been pursuing all these years; the Obsidian Sarcophagus. Other details about this artifact, or what the Nazi wraith's plans for it are, remain scarce. This has forced Reut to do the unthinkable; leave home, alone, without her living family's blessing. She's now travelling north, in search of both more information and allies.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A bespectacled young woman with brown hair down to her shoulders. She wears modest clothing, including long skirts and buttoned up blouses, in keeping with Hasidic beliefs. Despite her conservative appearance there's a certain intensity to Reut's hazel eyes, hinting at the medium's supernatural sight.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You seem lost, torn between what you've been taught a good woman's life should be and the task G*d has chosen you for. This insecurity leaves people with the impression that you're extremely shy. Even though you're certainly softspoken, afraid you are not. Cause acting in accordance with what you believe is G*d's plan inspires fearlessness. Only your family's disapproval keeps holding you back.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Fanatic<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Child<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 2, Manipulation 3, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 4, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 2, Awareness 3, Empathy 3, Expression 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Crafts 1, Etiquette 2, Larceny 1, Performance (Singing) 2, Stealth 2<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Occult 2<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 3, Contacts 2, Resources 1<br /> <b>Virtues:</b> Conscience 3, Self-Control 4, Courage 4<br /> <b>Morality:</b> Humanity 8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Language (Hebrew, Spanish + mother tongue Yiddish), Medium, Spirit Mentor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T23:15:38-07:00","id":1559026,"title":"","content":"<b>17. Henry Bates, weird weeaboo <i>Bleach</i> fan</b><br /> On a foggy autumn afternoon day on the 25th of March 2008, a college drop-out named Henry Bates got run over by a truck, while walking back home from his dead-end Walmart cashier job. He died in a very obscure part of the sidewalk by a major junction; most assuredly the truck driver at the time suspected he'd hit &quot;something&quot; that was more than just a &quot;raccoon,&quot; but chose to continue to drive down the road and not investigate further. Better to not rock the proverbial boat when he was already <i>so </i>behind schedule with freight. <br /> <br /> Henry's family had put up Missing Person posters everywhere to try and find him. The local police department was involved every step of the way for the first couple of weeks, but that eventually petered out as routine and more pressing issues arose. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile during that same span of time in the Shadowlands, Henry was inducted into a Heretic band than claimed him as soon as they gained an inkling of his possible demise. He grew well into the mentality of this particular band, as he was not frightened by this strange afterlife, but delighted by it; this newly discovered deathly world, so similar but at once entirely so alien.. greatly reminded him of <i>Bleach</i>, in some twisted sense.<br /> <br /> He quickly went on to develop his Arcanoi and learn two-handed sword fighting from a circlemember named Flori, a German mercenary soldier all the way from 1402 at the time of latter's death. Honorably serving for years with this band, he decided to amicably split from it and begin traveling the Shadowlands, and then greater Underworld itself alone for a while. Henry spent another bundle of years taking job after job, growing his skill and gaining (in)famous notoriety as he progressed. <br /> <br /> After completing a job in a small Necropolis outside of Baghdad, Henry learns from a darkened, fiery smiled, well-connected patron that the Jade Emperor that rules over Yellow Springs may actually be a Spectre of somesort.. not just any Spectre, but a Malfean of all things. Knowing from prior knowledge of how Yellow Springs controls most of the East Asian shadowlands, to learn of such a rumor... is deeply disturbing to Henry, given his awful encounters with the Spectres over the years. <br /> <br /> Feeling a sense of duty toward Japan, despite never setting a foot in it and only knowing it vicariously over the years from anime (and with the fact he hasn't watched much anime at all since his death in 2008), Henry decides to head over to the Shadowlands of Japan with one mission in mind; free it from Yellow Springs..<br /> <br /> <b>Image: </b>A young adult appearing man with black hair, glowing orange eye scleras with no irises or pupils, and greenish grey corpus skin. The only apparel he wears is a sleeveless robe over a soulsteel chainmail shirt and sandals, along with a scabbard at his back holding a two-handed style sword. <br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints: </b>You are an aimless, but hardened survivor of the Shadowlands of Earth, never sticking in one locale and always on the move when jobs peter away. This self-imposed quest you task yourself toward.. is spotty at best and completely nonsensical at the worst. But at least now you have something concrete.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature: </b>Zealot<br /> <b>Demeanor: </b>Outsider <br /> <br /> <b>Physical: </b>Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social: </b>Charisma 4, Manipulation 2, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Mental: </b>Perception 5, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <br /> <b>Talents: </b> Alertness 4, Awareness 4, Throwing 2, Unarmed 3, Dodge 5, Athletics 4, Leadership 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills: </b>Meditation 3, Melee 5, Stealth 4<br /> <b>Knowledges: </b>Enigmas 2, Investigation 4, Occult 2, Theology (Heretics) 2<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds: </b>Contacts 4, Eidolon 3, Notoriety 3<br /> <br /> <b>Arcanoi: </b>Outrage 4, Embody 4, Phantasm 3, Argos 2<br /> <b>Passion: </b>Destroy Spectres (Duty) 4, Watch Bleach (Joy) 3, Protect Cats (Love) 2, Haunt Retail Stores (Nostalgia) 1<br /> <b>Fetters: </b>Strange Roadside Skeleton 3, Abandoned Truck 3, Former Hot Walmart Manager 1<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower: </b>8<br /> <b>Pathos: </b>8<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus: </b>12<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow: </b>The Mastermind<br /> <b>Angst: </b>8<br /> <b>Thorns: </b>Tainted Relic (A one-handed katana completely different from his soulsteel two-handed straight sword... more sinister, more horrific in deathly eminence) 3, Spectre Prestige 2<br /> <b>Dark Passions: </b>Murder Truck Drivers (Vengeance) 4, Destroy Anime &amp; Manga (Self-Doubt) 3, Kill Cats (Power) 2, Kill Female Retail Store Managers (Amusement) 1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T15:16:23-07:00","id":1559609,"title":"","content":"One of my Wild West Giovanni PCs had to sacrifice a ghoul, so:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>18. Giorgio Putanesca, the elder brother</b><br /> The wraith of a recently killed Giovanni ghoul, now a European Premascine's spy. Now finally released of the blood bond, he wants to make his own attempts at intrigue.<br /> Giorgio had the distinct honor of being the first American born Putanesca. His dear brothers, Guido and Giuseppe, being two and three. While growing up in New York City they admired their Uncle Ennio, who the Giovanni rewarded with the Proxy Kiss for the criminal empire he was instrumental in building. When that uncle was finally promoted, from ghoul to vampire, Giorgio offered his services.<br /> The young man didn't like who he became after partaking of Ennio Putanesca's vitae, fearing the dark impulses it awakened in him. But unfortunately Giorgio proved unable to decline further offers of the blood, becoming a slave to it. When his undead master thought it time to induct his younger brothers, Giorgio helped convince them to become ghouls as well. The true love for his closest family defeated by the artificial devotion his undead uncle.<br /> In the fall of 1863 orders came from Europe, Ennio was to travel West with the other American Giovanni Kindred. After the train journey it was the Putanesca brothers who transported these vampires, by stagecoach, deep into the New Mexico Territory. It was along that path where Giorgio lost his life. Uncle Ennio had ordered his brothers, as to appease a disgruntled Clan elder, to cut his throat. The ancient Giovanni was waiting for Giorgio across the sudario, giving the wraith his new marching orders.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A Mediterranean man who became a ghoul when he was just twenty. As a wraith he appears in the dusty rider's garb, worn while crossing the New Mexico wilds, and a bowler hat that doesn't quite match. Giorgio's throat looks to be cut almost the entire way through. A gaping gash, still bleeding profusely, his soaked neckerchief has no hope of hiding. The man's handsome face is decorated by a moustache and prominent sideburns.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints: </b>In the afterlife you still carry yourself with all the bluster of a street tough. But beneath that hard exterior you're first and foremost a loving brother. Hence why you're hoping to incite other Giovanni against Ennio, in order to free your kin. Though the ambitious youngster who thought to improve his lot through ghouldom is still part of you as well. On this side of the Shroud you still see a future for yourself climbing the Giovanni ranks.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Caregiver<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Bravo<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 2, Manipulation 3, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 2, Athletics 1, Awareness 1, Brawl 2, Empathy 1, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 1, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Ride 2, Etiquette 1, Firearms 1, Larceny 2, Leadership 1, Melee 2, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Enigmas 1, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Politics 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Eidolon 3, Memoriam 2, Notoriety 1, Status 1<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Inhabit 3, Lifeweb 1 Outrage 1, Pandemonium 1, Phantasm 1<br /> <b>Passions:</b> Earn Clan Giovanni's respect (Pride) 3, Free brothers from servitude (Love) 5, Punish Ennio (Revenge) 2<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Ennio Putanesca 2, Giuseppe Putanesca 4, Guido Putanesca 4, Smith &amp; Wesson Revolver 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Pathos:</b> 8<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 10<br /> <b>Shadow:</b> The Abuser<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 4<br /> <b>Thorns:</b> Death's Sigil, Tainted Touch<br /> <b>Dark Passions:</b> Destroy Ennio Putanesca (Hate) 2, Kill brothers (Twisted Love) 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-07T14:56:12-07:00","id":1563901,"title":"","content":"One of the main antagonists in my Wild West chronicle:<br /> <br /> <b>19. Henri Corbeau, the manor phantom</b><br /> A Spectre who in life was Mesa Trueno's richest man. In death a lieutenant of the Thunderbird, who seeks to drag the town into Oblivion. Though Corbeau seems mostly preoccupied by his former home, remaining close to his daughter.<br /> Around 1800 Henri grew up on the streets of Paris, the child of a streetwalker and an unknown father. In order to escape poverty the boy joined Napoleon's Grande Arm\u00e9e at too young an age. The new recruit saw much death during the German campaign of 1813. When the Emperor finally abdicated Henri had his fill of war, and of France. The teen immigrated to the New World, arriving by ship in New Orleans.<br /> Once in Louisiana young Henri was once again as penniless as the day of his birth. He struggled to survive, America not being the land of easy wealth he'd hoped for. Henri had no one to rely on, until he met Laurent de Mer. He was a fellow Frenchman, who emigrated nearly two decades earlier. The older gentleman helped the young man get on his feet. But there was of course a price. Monsieur de Mer was an occultist who required assistance in performing his dark rites. For this new master the younger Frenchman would end up taking more lives than he did under Napoleon. When years later de Mer left him behind in New Orleans, for a move to the Pacific Coast, Henri was glad to be rid of the man and his Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon.<br /> Henri wouldn't hear from Laurent de Mer again, one last time, until 1849. In the intervening years he'd married Martha and together they had a daughter, M\u00e9lanie. They'd moved West, into what was to become the New Mexico Territory, where Corbeau dug for gold. But he had little success. Hence why he was preparing to leave Mesa Trueno, to join in the California goldrush. But then a letter arrived from his former master, instructing to dig in a specific spot, high up the mountain overlooking the mining camp. There Henri discovered the richest gold deposit of the region.<br /> Over the following year Henri lost no time utilizing the newfound wealth in consolidating his hold over Mesa Trueno's gold. Other miners either sold their claim or were dealt with by hired gunmen. While local Indian families were simply driven off their land. As Corbeau transformed the mountain, into a major goldmining enterprise, the camp at its foot grew into a proper town. Which was overshadowed on its far side by the construction of Corbeau Manor, where his family was to lead a life of affluence, though not necessarily happiness.<br /> Henri had always been overly protective of his daughter M\u00e9lanie. But as the girl entered her teens his feelings degenerated into those most improper for a father. He never acted on them, except by jealously hiding the young lady away from the world. The ever expanding mansion became M\u00e9lanie's gilded cage, while her father pursued release to his frustrations in the town below.<br /> During one of his visits to the local brothel Henri met a true lady of the night; the vampiress Mocel. No chance encounter, the undead beauty had deliberately sought out the town's most powerful man. By enthralling Corbeau she managed to become Mesa Trueno's true mistress. Even going so far as placing her haven in secret passages beneath the manor.<br /> Unfortunately for him Mocel wasn't the only supernatural being who wished to control Corbeau. In 1860 the Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon, although Laurent de Mer was apparently gone, had come to collect on their past aid. His goldmine was to expand further into the burial sites of the local Akimel O'odham tribe. Henri, knowing the society, dared not refuse their request.<br /> The dynamiting of the indigenous sacred site was preceded by a short speech and ceremony, attended by Corbeau's wife and employees. The subsequent blasts were met with cheers. But in his soul Henri had already known something was amiss, moments before the ground started shaking. Subsequently came the avalanche, which hardly anyone present survived. He arrived in the Shadowlands amidst a Maelstrom, with the Thunderbird soaring overhead. There were Spectres everywhere. Henri Corbeau's Shadow made sure he joined them soon enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> An imposing skeletal figure, wearing a dark suit, overcoat and top hat. Henri's eye sockets are burning with a luminescent darkness. The only real color his Corpus shows is a purple necktie. True to the Corbeau name he regularly spies on the Skinlands by Puppeteering a raven.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You've often felt misunderstood. You were no monster, but simply a man trying to provide for his family and build a town. As a Spectre you've become the villain everyone considered you to be. Appearing most amused by people's misfortune, laughing menacingly at their terror. You say little though, cause it's no longer your place to give speeches. The Thunderbird is who you serve. You'll present him with every soul in Mesa Trueno. Only sweet M\u00e9lanie you'll keep for yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Conniver<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Bon Vivant<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 2, Manipulation 4, Appearance 0<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 3, Intelligence 3, Wits 4<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 1, Athletics 1, Awareness 1, Brawl 2, Expression 1, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 1, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Crafts 1, Etiquette 1, Firearms 2, Larceny 1, Leadership 2, Melee 2, Ride 1, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Bureaucracy 1, Occult 2, Politics 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Contacts 2, Haunt 5, Legacy 2, Memoriam 4, Mentor 3, Shadowlands 2 Status 2<br /> <b>Arcanoi:</b> Collogue 2, Pandemonium 4, Puppetry 4, Shroud Rending 2<br /> <b>Dark Passions:</b> Haunt M\u00e9lanie (Lust) 3, Isolate M\u00e9lanie (Jealousy) 5, Serve up Mesa Trueno's souls to the Thunderbird (Contempt) 2<br /> <b>Fetters:</b> Corbeau Manor 2, M\u00e9lanie 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Permanent Corpus:</b> 9<br /> <b>Angst:</b> 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}